WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.804
The numbers that matter: GeoReasoner improves on
the best comparable vision-language model

00:00:05.884 --> 00:00:11.361
by twenty-five point zero two percent at the
country level and thirty-eight point six

00:00:11.441 --> 00:00:13.714
one percent at the city level in F1.

00:00:13.794 --> 00:00:19.990
Its full-model F1 scores are zero point nine zero
for country and zero point eight six for city.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:23.913
It achieves this with just seventy thousand
training images,

00:00:23.993 --> 00:00:29.404
versus the one point one million used by
StreetCLIP, which it nonetheless surpasses.

00:00:29.484 --> 00:00:34.961
The underlying data comes from more than one
hundred thirty thousand raw street views

00:00:35.041 --> 00:00:38.360
across seventy-two cities and forty-eight countries,

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.583
filtered down to seventy thousand,

00:00:40.663 --> 00:00:44.833
plus three thousand human-written reasoning clues
from geo-games.

00:00:44.913 --> 00:00:47.055
And on the open Im2GPS benchmarks,

00:00:47.135 --> 00:00:52.220
only ten thousand Flickr images are enough to rival
models trained on millions.
